## The hall

::bg{location="pebbleton-museum" time="day"}
::music{playback="start" mood="calm" volume="down"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: The Pebbleton Museum of Old Things. The hall is cool and smells of polish. In the middle, under glass, a fossil the size of a kite: two stone wings, spread.
::actor{character="pebbletonCurator" anchor="center" action="enter"}
@pebbletonCurator{code="0010" emotion="happy"}: A visitor! Welcome, welcome. I'm Ottoline, the curator. That's our wing fossil. Seventy million years old and it still looks cross about something.
@pebbletonCurator{code="0020"}: We used to have dome and spiral fossils too, from the old workings in Moonstone Cave. Lovely things. The seams were thought to be exhausted.
@pebbletonCurator{code="0030" emotion="surprised"}: And now the miners say somebody is digging down there at night. With lights. And crates.
@pebbletonCurator{code="0040"}: If you're passing through the cave, and if a fossil happened to come home with you, Dr. Kell in the back room would give her eye teeth to see it. She thinks she can bring them back. To life, I mean. Don't laugh.
::accept{quest="southFossil"}
::actor{character="pebbletonCurator" action="exit"}
